From 4fbbf7bdec4bd8ea3edca6083c387cc46791c578 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 21:02:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(ai): bound the Ollama model selection and name each
 failure cause

The automatic selection stopped at the first failed /api/show probe and
used the 300 s chat time limit for each request. Now a failed probe of
one model does not stop the selection, each request has a 5 s limit and
the whole selection has a 20 s limit. Each cause has its own message:
the server did not answer its model list, no installed model can call
tools, the probe failed for a named model, or the time limit ended. A
chat failure after an automatic selection names the selected model.

The loopback fixture sets its accepted socket to blocking mode. On
macOS the socket inherited the nonblocking mode of the listener and the
fixture failed at times.

Refs #3782

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
